{
  "$comment": "JSON Schema draft-07. Local references only. Structural validation is necessary but never verifies cryptography, trust, authorization, provider qualification or current acceptance under independently configured policy. Reject duplicate members/trailing bytes and enforce depth <=16, UTF-8 byte limits (ordinary strings <=256), HTTP limits and canonical encodings before validation. External checks include JWK thumbprints, JCS hashes, equality of projected/bound/enrolled identities, ASCII-only host canonicalization, time ordering/lifetimes/key validity, nonce consumption, policy-required checks, release eligibility/digest equality, status sequence/withdrawal and independent trust settings. Ed25519 verification is strict: reject non-canonical S, non-canonical R or public-key encodings and small-order R points or public keys. Times are exclusive at expiry (valid while now < expires_at) and inclusive at not_before. Evidence/status lifetime <=60 seconds; assessment expiry <=observed_from+900, issued_at<=observed_until+60; key validity <=90 days; challenge expiry <=issued_at+600. No schema alone establishes these relationships. Assessment expiry must not exceed independently authorized operator-record, enrollment, publisher-key or verifier-key expiry. Current status expiry must not exceed those bounds, assessment expiry or issued_at+60. Recheck authority at publication/commit and status reuse even when authorization generation is unchanged; expired operator authority stops positive assessment/current status. Configuration checks concern signed publisher-declared identity/enrollment consistency only, never a registry read of full configuration. Default acceptance is expiry-only (require_status=false); live status is an optional stricter policy. A cached positive consumer result never outlives the earliest accepted-threshold assessment expiry, independently configured trust-key acceptance deadline, original observation time plus configured observation age, evaluated_at plus configured cache lifetime, or required live-status expiry and original issued_at plus configured status maximum age (at most 60 seconds); expiry-only acceptance adds no status-expiry dependency. Non-null operator identity requires independent exact operator DNS/account proof; null denotes self-operated with no distinct operator claim.",
  "title": "Publisher attestation version 1 structural contract",
